2026-06-22 21:45:25,707 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 21:45:25,708 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To meet the client's requirements, we will implement the following key security and compliance measures. 

Firstly, our ISO 27001 certification, which we have held since 2023, demonstrates our commitment to information security management. This certification covers the development, delivery, and operations of our services.

Regarding data protection, our ISO 27701 certification provides a framework for privacy information management. This extension to ISO 27001 ensures that we can manage personal data in accordance with GDPR principles.

To ensure the confidentiality and integrity of client data, we will utilize encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. Our key management infrastructure is based in the EU, ensuring that sensitive data remains within the region.

We will also implement strict partitioning of client files, with logical isolation per client and per mission, to prevent any cross-client circulation of data. Access controls will be enforced through role-based access control (RBAC) and audit logging, which logs every system output and access event.

Given that our hosting partner is OuraneCloud, which holds the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer, we can guarantee sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU. This aligns with the client's requirement for data to be hosted within the EU and not transferred outside the EU.

To comply with GDPR, we have appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO) and maintain a data processing register. Our data protection agreement (DPA) is aligned with GDPR Article 28, ensuring that all data processing activities are compliant with relevant regulations.

Additionally, our experience working with clients bound by professional secrecy, including national professional orders, demonstrates our familiarity with the importance of confidentiality and data protection in sensitive environments.

Our security controls include secure software development lifecycle practices such as code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing conducted by an external provider equivalent to CREST level. We also have a vulnerability management process in place with remediation SLAs based on severity, ensuring timely response to potential security issues.

In the event of a breach, our incident response plan includes detection, notification, and remediation procedures, aligned with the 72-hour GDPR breach notification requirement.

Lastly, our Atelier product is designed with explainability and auditability in mind, providing features such as retrieval trace, audit log, and figure source linking. This supports internal quality control and statutory audit review, ensuring that all outputs are grounded in sources and can be traced back to their origin.

By implementing these measures, we can ensure the strict respect of professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data, comply with GDPR requirements, and provide a secure environment for hosting and processing sensitive information within the EU.
