The solution will provide an intelligent assistance tool accessible from the firm's professionals' work environment, supporting them in their daily activities. This tool will assist with retrieval of regulatory and methodological information, drafting professional documents, handling client files, and facilitating mission continuity between collaborators. Our hybrid retrieval capabilities combine lexical and semantic search to efficiently locate relevant information within the client's documentation.

To ensure integration with existing practices, our solution will be designed to fit into Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' current working methods without introducing any disruptions. The chartered accountant or statutory auditor remains the sole validator, and no deliverable is produced or signed without professional validation. Our template-guided drafting capability will support drafting professional documents such as client letters and correspondence, mission notes, file memos, and syntheses.

Our proposed technical architecture is based on Atelier, which can be integrated with various business tools. We will use API-first design to integrate the platform with accounting-production software, payroll software, document management/GED, and electronic-invoicing/dematerialization environment. The solution will be deployed on a cloud infrastructure that can scale horizontally, ensuring high availability during business hours and resilience to seasonal peak loads.

To address security and compliance concerns, we have implemented strict measures to ensure the confidentiality and integrity of client data. Our ISO 27001 certification demonstrates our commitment to information security management, while our ISO 27701 certification provides a framework for privacy information management. We utilize encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, with key management infrastructure based in the EU.

Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, is SecNumCloud-qualified, ensuring sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU. We have also implemented strict partitioning of client files, logical isolation per client and per mission, and access controls enforced through role-based access control (RBAC) and audit logging.

In terms of budget, our engagement of €220,000 over 3 years is well within our financial capacity. We estimate that one-off project costs will account for around 40% of the total budget, while recurring run costs will account for about 60%. Our daily rates will be used to estimate the number of days required for each type of consultant.

To optimize costs while ensuring the expected quality of service, we propose a cost-efficient approach that prioritizes our sovereign tier with the European model. This option minimizes hosting and inference expenses, which are identified as main recurring cost drivers.

Our company, Faber IA, is committed to respecting professional secrecy and auditor independence. As a Société par actions simplifiée (SAS) registered in France, we must ensure that our licensing terms are compatible with the requirements of respecting auditor independence and separation of duties.

We also prioritize environmental considerations, aiming to limit the environmental footprint of the solution and rely on low-carbon infrastructure as far as possible. Our green hosting partner, OuraneCloud, offers sovereign hosting in the EU, renewable energy, a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and heat reuse, which can help reduce the environmental footprint of the solution.

Our AI innovation elements include Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities, hybrid retrieval capabilities, template-guided drafting, explainability tools, and fine-tuning methods. These features will provide an intelligent assistance tool that improves productivity, quality, and reliability while ensuring explainability and transparency.

In conclusion, our consortium proposes a comprehensive solution that meets Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' requirements for an artificial intelligence assistance solution. Our Atelier platform, combined with our technical architecture, security measures, and cost-efficient approach, will provide a high-quality service that respects professional secrecy and auditor independence while minimizing the environmental footprint of the solution.
